.TH "CSDLC-REVIEW" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-review \- validate independent exact\-head review evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc review ISSUE \-\-evidence REVIEW.json
\&csdlc review \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
\&csdlc review \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The semantic issue intent form is the current operational interface. It resolves issue identity and routes effects through the native semantic transaction owner.
.PP
\&The intent form validates and retains externally supplied independent exact\-head review. REVIEW.json contains receipt, receipt_digest, proof_path and proof_digest. The receipt includes reviewed publication_linkage; proof binds exact candidate bytes and issue version. The ordinary form writes create\-only external evidence and native review records; \-\-preview plan is read\-only. Legacy \-\-request review admission remains observational.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share identity and mutation guards.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Checks that implementer/reviewer are not the same nonempty principal and that a review revision is supplied. The current review classifier does not authenticate the typed receipt contents or perform the human/subagent review; loading a receipt is not evidence that this route validated it. Independent review and a matching typed receipt remain required by policy and later publication checks. Without \-\-execute produces a non\-authoritative plan; with it requires operational envelope operation.kind review and authenticated authority.
.SH OPTIONS
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-observe\-github: Perform authenticated GitHub readback. Requires selected credentials. It does not itself create, update or merge a PR.
.PP
\&\-\-execute: Select typed operational dispatch, not a generic force flag. Cannot combine with \-\-observe\-github on non\-pr\-state remote routes.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.PP
\&\-\-intent\-request: Execute an exact generated csdlc.v3.intent_request.v1 request or its generated wrapper; stale snapshots fail closed.
.SH REQUEST
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Without \-\-execute: RemoteRouteRequest, including typed review/readback receipt references when required. With \-\-execute on non\-pr\-state: OperationalRemoteDispatchRequest, whose expected_lifecycle_digest is the canonical authority selector payload digest, not the local issue index digest. See csdlc\-requests(1).
.PP
\&Non\-pr\-state \-\-execute plus \-\-observe\-github is rejected. \-\-observe\-github without \-\-execute uses authenticated readback in the planning path; it does not turn the returned plan into a performed mutation. Request family must match the selected mode.
.SH EFFECTS
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Readback/planning does not perform remote mutation. Operational github mutation writes durable intent before network dispatch and retains authenticated reconciliation/receipt. Successful review/publish plan reports are not PR creation. Credential names are scoped to the adapter; no raw token in argv or request.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.nf
\&csdlc review 870 \-\-evidence review\-evidence.json
.fi
.PP
\&Request fixtures are in docs/csdlc\-v3/man/examples/; values are illustrative and must be bound to the actual head and reviewed issue. See csdlc\-workflow(1) for the full live sequence.
.SH RECOVERY
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&After uncertain dispatch retain the original request and exact intent. Reinvoke the identical native request for authenticated reconciliation. A changed request is a different operation, not a retry. Never delete the target guard or intent to force a second write.
.PP
\&Issue\-edit does not support write replay, including retry_after_authenticated_absence; reconcile exact retained target and preserve later human changes. Supported create/ready absence retry is explicit, authenticated and one\-shot. Merge retries are always read\-only; a still\-open or uncertain PR remains blocked.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1), csdlc\-finish(1).
